# Frappe Development

When generating Frappe code, follow `AGENTS.md` and the skills under `skills/`
in this frappe-skills repo (`.cursor/frappe-skills/`).

## Before coding

1. Read [AGENTS.md](../AGENTS.md) for skills activation and the canonical
   custom-app layout.
2. Read only the `SKILL.md` / reference files the current task needs.

## Skills — when to activate

| Skill | When to Read |
| ----- | ------------ |
| `frappe-app-dev` | Any Frappe/bench task (DocTypes, controllers, APIs, hooks, permissions, jobs, tests, bench CLI) — [SKILL.md](../skills/frappe-app-dev/SKILL.md) |
| `code-style` | Writing or editing Python/JS — [SKILL.md](../skills/code-style/SKILL.md) |
| `ui-design` | Desk UI, Vue SPA, portal, or front-end UX — [SKILL.md](../skills/ui-design/SKILL.md) |
| `quality-code-review` | Explicit code review; also run its §0 hygiene checklist before ending any file-creating/editing task — [SKILL.md](../skills/quality-code-review/SKILL.md) |

- **Always** Read `code-style` when writing or editing Python or JavaScript.
- **Always** Read `frappe-app-dev` for any Frappe/bench task.
- Do **not** Read all skills at once.

## frappe-app-dev flow

After Reading `frappe-app-dev` SKILL.md, pick one flow:

- New app → `references/new-app.md`, then complete tooling per
  [custom-app.mdc](./custom-app.mdc) (source:
  [custom_app_setup.md](../project_base_template/custom_app_setup.md))
- Existing app → `references/existing-app.md`

Then load only the feature references needed (doctypes, controllers, api,
hooks, etc.) — see the table in AGENTS.md.
